  "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nFix facing's false \"two holes\" refusal on concave cutouts. A missing scanline piece does not prove a narrow strip between separate holes: both crossings can belong to a return of the same boundary.\r\n\r\n- Retain boundary-loop identity with each crossing and require distinct boundaries, a positive gap no wider than the cutter, and a missing row piece before issuing the inter-hole refusal.\r\n- Preserve the existing radius-grown clipping, row geometry, swept-area leftover notes, and post-verification. Concave returns remain clipped; they are not driven through to manufacture a successful path.\r\n- Retain genuinely narrow and exactly-tool-width inter-hole refusals. Add wide/narrow U-notch regressions in both cutting directions, including cutter-radius-clearance checks.\r\n- Record the decision in `docs/decisions/260-facing-gap.md`.\r\n\r\n## Readings and diagnosis\r\n\r\nThe #260 report and attached `cutouts.camproj`, the facing generator and hole clipping code, `Region`'s normalized-loop contract, and the repository contribution/test rules. The reported 15.15 mm gap and a later 2.65 mm gap are concave returns of individual cutouts, not separate holes. A width-only guard was insufficient; boundary identity is necessary. No vendor implementation or assets were consulted.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nVerified commit: `b3dd4934090d6d30e17a1130939f6789799f8f2a` (tree `3d36ac1b75e3224022cdead91dbd77ad22baa366`), based on `1e60b2399dff677d9f44b143a24e626d268340f0`.\r\n\r\nNative Windows/MSVC checks:\r\n\r\n- Canonical `scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier quick -Base 1e60b2399dff677d9f44b143a24e626d268340f0`: **173 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored**, native exit 0. Motion library plus `center_cut_owed`, `face_blend`, `face_concave_holes`, and `face_holes`; gate-created logs and assertion summaries verified.\r\n- `cargo clippy --locked -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.\r\n- `rustfmt --edition 2024 --check crates/motion/tests/face_concave_holes.rs` and whitespace checks: passed.\r\n- Pinning tests: `a_wide_concave_gap_generates_and_reports_the_unfaced_return`, `a_narrow_concave_return_is_not_a_gap_between_separate_holes`, and `a_gap_exactly_one_tool_wide_still_refuses_when_no_row_piece_fits`. These are included in the quick-gate count above.\r\n- Sensitivity: the exact narrow-notch regression fails against the prior diameter-only implementation, then passes with boundary identity restored.\r\n- An asserted temporary app probe loaded the original public attachment and generated default Lift facing: **725 moves**, with the truthful **1653.05 mm^2 unfaced** and lift-over-holes notes. Trace, Through, and Contour controls also generated. The fixture's existing rotated-stock/rapid-law diagnostics were retained, not suppressed.\r\n- Independent static review: passed, no actionable findings.\r\n\r\n## Limits\r\n\r\nThis fixes false rejection, not complete facing coverage: material reported unfaced remains unfaced. No Linux/macOS execution, interactive GUI test, full batch/release/heavy lanes, or real-machine validation is claimed. No workflow was dispatched, release produced, or NC output transferred to a machine. Broader #241 selection/box-picking symptoms and #261 error-path visualization are outside this change.\r\n\r\nChangelog: Facing distinguishes concave returns within one cutout from genuinely narrow gaps between separate hole boundaries, preserving clipping and unfaced-area notes.\r\n\r\nFixes #260\r\n",
